<blockquote class="uncited"><div>might be silly question can install the this code plug into the original  firmware ?</div></blockquote>No. <br><br>The OpenGD77 codeplug format is based on the Radioddity GD-77 codeplug format, and is still probably compatibile with the official Radioddity GD-77 CPS and firmware.<br><br>All other supported radios use completely different codeplug formats when running their official firmware.<br><br>The offical CPS sometimes have CSV export and import for Channels and other sections, but these also vary from radio to radio, and the OpenGD77 CSV export functionality is unlikely to be directly compatible with the official CPS CSV.<br>However, you could probably manually cut and paste the columns from the OpenGD77 CPS Channels.csv into the CSV for another radio and eventually transfer all the channel names and frequencies, if you have a lot of time on your hands<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Tue Dec 17, 2024 5:48 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
